# EdminBoost Compliance

Gate before presenting final code. If any checklist item is "no", fix it first.

See `edminboost-project.mdc` (architecture), `edminboost-standards.mdc` (quality), `edminboost-command-center.mdc` (Command Center), `wordpress-php.mdc` (PHP patterns).

## Security

- Sanitize on input, escape on output, authorize before action, verify nonce before write.
- Never trust browser, REST, AJAX, cron, or webhook input.
- Use `EDMINBOOST_Settings::CAPABILITY` on admin pages and in `sanitize()`.
- Settings API: `sanitize_callback`, `show_in_rest => false`, `wp_unslash()` on array input.
- Custom forms/AJAX: `wp_nonce_field()` + `check_admin_referer()` / `wp_verify_nonce()`.
- CC drawer iframe loads: verify `_wpnonce` against `edminboost_cc_drawer_{md5(slug + anchor)}` and whitelist slug+anchor via `is_drawer_slug_allowed()` (or `edminboost_mapper_preview=1` from Layout Studio) before stripping admin chrome.
- CC drawer preview AJAX (`edminboost_cc_drawer_preview`): `current_user_can( CAPABILITY )`, `check_ajax_referer( 'edminboost_cc_drawer_preview' )`, `is_mapper_preview_context()`, validate slug via `is_valid_drawer_slug()`.
- Settings save AJAX (`edminboost_save_settings`): `current_user_can( CAPABILITY )`, verify nonce against `EDMINBOOST_Settings::SETTINGS_GROUP . '-options'`, sanitize via `EDMINBOOST_Settings::sanitize()` before `update_option()`.
- CC tab navigation AJAX (`edminboost_load_cc_page`): `current_user_can( CAPABILITY )`, `check_ajax_referer( 'edminboost_cc_nav' )`, validate `page` via `EDMINBOOST_Admin::is_valid_cc_nav_page()` (whitelist from `EDMINBOOST_Command_Center::get_nav_items()`); render server-side HTML only — no raw partial paths from the client.
- SQL: `$wpdb->prepare()` only; prefer Options API (`edminboost_*`) over custom tables.

## Directory & Privacy

- No obfuscated code, undisclosed telemetry, or hidden external requests.
- No tracking or data transmission to external servers (current plugin behavior).
- Badge sources (WooCommerce orders, comments, updates, WPForms entries) read local WordPress data only — no remote API calls. WPForms count uses a guarded `$wpdb` read when the plugin and table exist.
- No public-site credit injection by default (admin footer replacement is opt-in).
- No spammy readme, deceptive "free" behavior, or fake trial logic.
- Any future remote integration must be documented, justified, and opt-in.

## Code Quality

- Prefer WordPress core APIs over custom hacks.
- Keep code human-readable for directory review.
- Follow WPCS across PHP, CSS, JS, and HTML.
- Admin-only unless explicitly requested; enqueue plugin-screen assets via `is_plugin_screen()`; visual theme CSS (`edminboost-themes`), CC bar CSS/JS, and drawer shell are the allowed front-end exceptions when active.
- Use `edminboost` prefix (10 chars) consistently — `EDMINBOOST_` / `edminboost_`.

## Self-Review Checklist

- [ ] No WordPress core modifications
- [ ] GPL-compatible
- [ ] Human-readable, reviewable code
- [ ] User-facing strings translatable (`EDMINBOOST_TEXT_DOMAIN`)
- [ ] Privileged actions: capability checks + nonces
- [ ] Input sanitized; output escaped
- [ ] SQL prepared (if any)
- [ ] Assets scoped; admin notices minimal and dismissible
- [ ] No tracking without explicit consent; remotes documented
- [ ] Public credits disabled by default; no trialware
- [ ] Uninstall path removes plugin data safely
- [ ] Unique `EDMINBOOST_` / `edminboost_` prefix; maintainable structure
- [ ] Would survive WordPress.org review

## Unsafe Requests

If a feature conflicts with the Plugin Handbook, Coding Standards, security best practices, privacy expectations, or Directory Guidelines — refuse the unsafe approach and propose a compliant alternative.
